        "id": 1003023
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T07:17:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a provider constructor is assigned another module-level name, including after loading it from a frozen module, `export_as` runs again and replaces `data`; for example, `AliasInfo \u003d OriginalInfo` changes existing `OriginalInfo(...)` instances to print and report their type as `AliasInfo`.\n\nI think this also invalidates the `Sync` safety claim because parallel evaluations can read the old parameter spec while another evaluation drops it. We somehow need to make the initialization one-shot and ensure that subsequent exports don\u0027t mutate the provider...\n\nI\u0027ll add some suggested edits for an approach using `std::sync::OnceLock\u003cProviderTypeData\u003e` that I think might work and would let us remove this three line unsafe block here - let me know what you think.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "aa5e17ede5ded1d09336345e313fea3e5fb790b4",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ebed4d25_a3ab932f",
        "filename": "src/gn/starlark/crates/providers/src/provider_type.rs",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 3810482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T08:59:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wasn\u0027t aware that export_as ran multiple times, thanks for catching that.\n\nI wanted to avoid a solution which involves a lock when creating new instances of a provider. So I\u0027ve refactored the design to ensure that frozen values are immutable while avoiding locking.",
      "parentUuid": "34d08457_a9c258e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "aa5e17ede5ded1d09336345e313fea3e5fb790b4",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
