      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mhm, OK, I see. I would usually say \"let\u0027s benchmark before (and after) optimizing\", but if you feel strongly about it, let\u0027s try to do it lock-free. Do you think there\u0027s a way we could achieve it without relying on module identity? Maybe by following Starlark\u0027s `RecordType` representation?\n\nI\u0027ll add a few ideas for this in the other comments, but we\u0027re way outside my Rust knowledge and comfort zone - if you really think this is the best way, then I\u0027m fine if Cole also thinks it\u0027s OK.",
